<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Conclusion</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work studied the energy efficiency maximization problem for UAV-enabled data collection in IoT networks. The resource allocation subproblem was transformed into an equivalent linear programming and solved optimally, while the UAV trajectory control problem was reformulated as an offline RL problem. To overcome the reliance of expert-quality data and large-scale training in existing DT methods, we proposed an LLM-empowered critic-regularized DT framework, i.e., LLM-CRDT, to learn effective UAV control policies from a offline dataset. LLM-CRDT integrates critic-based value guidance into DT training, enabling effective policy learning from suboptimal data. Moreover, a pre-trained LLM was adopted as the transformer backbone of LLM-CRDT, and LoRA-based fine-tuning was employed to enable rapid adaptation to UAV control with small datasets and low computational overhead. Simulations demonstrated that LLM-CRDT significantly outperforms benchmark online and offline RL approaches.</p>
</div>
<section id="A0.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A0.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">-A</span> </span><span id="A0.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ III-B Problem Transformation and Analysis ‣ III Optimal Resource Allocation and Problem Transformation ‣ Large Language Model-Empowered Decision Transformer for UAV-Enabled Data Collection" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_upright"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="A0.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove Theorem <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ III-B Problem Transformation and Analysis ‣ III Optimal Resource Allocation and Problem Transformation ‣ Large Language Model-Empowered Decision Transformer for UAV-Enabled Data Collection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we first introduce a bound that characterizes the performance gap between return-conditioned supervised learning methods (such as DT) and their underlying behavior policy.
Consider the MDP formulated in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="III-B Problem Transformation and Analysis ‣ III Optimal Resource Allocation and Problem Transformation ‣ Large Language Model-Empowered Decision Transformer for UAV-Enabled Data Collection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III-B</span></a>, an unknown behaviour policy <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a conditioning function <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assuming the following conditions:</p>
<ol id="A0.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A0.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A0.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\bm{\tau})=\sum\nolimits_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\bm{\tau})=\sum\nolimits_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total return of a trajectory <math id="A0.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. For all initial state <math id="A0.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{1}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditioning function satisfy <math id="A0.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left(g({\bm{\tau}})=f(\bm{s}_{1})\left|\bm{s}_{1}\right.\right)\geq\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left(g({\bm{\tau}})=f(\bm{s}_{1})\left|\bm{s}_{1}\right.\right)\geq\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MDP is <math id="A0.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-deterministic, i.e., <math id="A0.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left(r_{t}\neq\mathcal{R}(\bm{s}_{t},\bm{a}_{t})~{\rm{or}}~\bm{s}_{t+1}\neq\mathcal{P}(\bm{s}_{t},\bm{a}_{t})\left|\bm{s}_{t},\bm{a}_{t}\right.\right)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>or</mi><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left(r_{t}\neq\mathcal{R}(\bm{s}_{t},\bm{a}_{t})~{\rm{or}}~\bm{s}_{t+1}\neq\mathcal{P}(\bm{s}_{t},\bm{a}_{t})\left|\bm{s}_{t},\bm{a}_{t}\right.\right)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> at all <math id="A0.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for the reward function <math id="A0.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and environment dynamics <math id="A0.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The conditioning function is consistent of the RTG, i.e., <math id="A0.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\bm{s}_{t})=f(\bm{s}_{t+1})+r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\bm{s}_{t})=f(\bm{s}_{t+1})+r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A0.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, the RCSL methods trained on data generated by the behavior policy <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following performance bound:</p>
<table id="A0.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]\leq\varepsilon\Big(\frac{1}{\zeta}+2\Big)T^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ζ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]\leq\varepsilon\Big(\frac{1}{\zeta}+2\Big)T^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the policy learned by RCSL methods when conditioned on function <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.
The proof of this bound is provided in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>.
Given an offline datset <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> collected by the behaviour policy <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we choose the conditioning function as <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(\bm{s}_{1})=\sum\nolimits_{r_{1:T}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}(\bm{s}_{1})}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\bm{s}_{1})=\sum\nolimits_{r_{1:T}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}(\bm{s}_{1})}r</annotation></semantics></math> and substitute it into (<a href="#A0.E41" title="In -A Proof of Theorem ‣ VI Conclusion ‣ Large Language Model-Empowered Decision Transformer for UAV-Enabled Data Collection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A0.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\Big[\sum\nolimits_{r_{1:T}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}(\bm{s}_{1})}r\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>r</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\Big[\sum\nolimits_{r_{1:T}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}(\bm{s}_{1})}r\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}}\Big[\sum\nolimits_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}}\Big[\sum\nolimits_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then recall the reward-to-go <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}_{t}=\sum\nolimits_{i=t}^{T}r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}_{t}=\sum\nolimits_{i=t}^{T}r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is obvious that the conditioning function <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\bm{s}_{t})=\hat{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\bm{s}_{t})=\hat{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the requirement about the consistence of conditioning function, i.e., condition 3). Thus, we have</p>
<table id="A0.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1})\right]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>RCSL</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1}}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1})\right]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{f}^{\rm{RCSL}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\!=\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\bm{\theta}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\!=\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\rm{B}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\tau}\sim\pi_{\bm{\theta}}}\left[g(\bm{\tau})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon\Big(\frac{1}{\zeta}+2\Big)T^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ζ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon\Big(\frac{1}{\zeta}+2\Big)T^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the learned policy of DT.
Thus, the proof is completed.</p>
</div>
</section>
